 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope` in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It's the equivalent of Flask's `with_appcontext`. It loads the app and pushes `app.app_context()` around your callback.\n\n- You usually don't need to apply it by hand. Commands registered via `@app.cli.command()` or `@bundle.cli.command()` are on an `AppGroup` (`src/tessel/app.py:338`, `src/tessel/bundles.py:49`), and `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:413`) wraps them automatically.\n- Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n- Use the decorator explicitly only on a plain `click` command or group that isn't an `AppGroup`.\n\n**App loader:** `LaunchInfo.load_app()` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`, method at line 333). It uses `create_app`, `--app`/`TESSEL_APP`, or falls back to `wsgi.py`/`app.py`. `TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`) is the top-level group that creates the `LaunchInfo`.\n\nExample in `tests/test_cli.py:306`, docs in `docs/cli.rst`.",
